[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\), where \(\theta\) is a real number. Then we can substitute \(z\) into the expression and find the real part.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m First, let's express \(z\) and \(\frac{1}{z}\) in terms of \(\theta\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m \[ z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m \[ \frac{1}{z} = \frac{1}{4e^{i\theta}} = \frac{1}{4}e^{-i\theta} = \frac{1}{4}(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m Now we can substitute these into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m \[ (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m \[ \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta - 96i\sin\theta + 144i\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) = \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m Combining these, the expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m \[ 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m \[ = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta) + i(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) + \frac{1}{4}(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)) \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=49749)[0m \[ = 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(300\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta + 36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta) \]
